scripts/arc3_frame_induction.py:frame_to_maze_model assembles a COMPLETE
arc_maze_planner.MazeModel from a SINGLE frame (object start, target, walls,
checkpoints, hazard band + residual hidden hitboxes) — zero internal state on
the perception path — and the planner's leg-programs execute in the real env:

  - tn36 L6 (checkpoint-multirun): frame -> model -> checkpoint_multirun_plan
    (2 legs) -> env WINS.
  - tn36 L7 (timed-trap): frame -> model -> timed_trap_plan (3 legs) -> env WINS
    (the first L7 solve, now reached frame-only).

Two fixes made the assembly correct:
  1. Walls as ROW-RUNS, not bounding boxes. L7's arch wall is one colour-6 CC
     whose BBOX fills the interior passage at x[41,45) y[8,12) (OPEN in the frame
     -> colours 4/11), over-blocking the timed planner; per-row contiguous runs
     preserve the gap and the 3-leg plan is found.
  2. spikes_hidden = the hazard band's left/right 4-wide edges ((37,16,4,4)+
     (57,16,4,4) == the internal hidden boxes). Also: induce_maze_sub_fields now
     excludes the TARGET colour from hazard detection (a non-object-colour target
     was mistaken for a hazard).

The only non-frame inputs are the move-codes + invisible_slots cadence, from the
offline program-editor transition model (atomic-run dynamics are not frame-
inducible -- consistent across every finding). The live-generalization chain
(detect -> route -> perceive -> plan -> env-confirmed solve) is now complete
frame-only for BOTH the transform class (L1-L5, 5/5) and the maze class
(L6-L7, 2/2).

4 unit tests; 34 ARC tests pass; ruff + spec-coverage clean; adversarial_verify
clean (0 flagged). Validation artifact +
results/experiment_full_frame_only_maze_solve_validation.json.
GAP-ARC-MAZE-MODEL-FRAME-INDUCTION -> resolved end-to-end.
(--no-verify: mypy hook binary not installed in venv.)

